  message: "SATISFIED ON THE FILED INSTANCES (PR #1155, dev bec1607e18). Re-ran the item's own repros on the merged tree:\n  JS fixture through analyze_javascript: process.cwd -> host_info_read, process.on -> ipc_recv, process.send -> ipc_send, process.nextTick -> None; method_starved_modules [] (was ['process']).\n  python fixture through analyze_python: ctypes.cdll.LoadLibrary -> fs_read; method_starved_modules [] (was ['ctypes.cdll']).\n  Surveys express, mobx, ioredis, jotai, EventEmitter2, killbill: starved [] on all six (each was ['process']).\nverify-claims A/B, pinned worktrees 494eb2f480 vs b9dfdb5f83, generic-taint-claims on express/mobx/ioredis: all 21 verdicts identical. express's details now name the real blocker (10 uncatalogued modules) instead of the false process starvation. The mobx/ioredis analyzer-blind caveat counts 29 method-kind primitives, down from 31 (process.on/send are seen). Classification counts on 9 JS-bearing surveys are unchanged.\nTHE GENERAL STATEMENT IS NOT ASSERTED. No guard checks the contradiction itself; filed as the residual. The from-import form cdll.LoadLibrary still does not classify; that is WI-torin's shape."  # 9ae0
